# CronCal needs none of these: with nothing set, its setup screens connect
# your Supabase project and keep the keys in the app-data folder (README,
# "Connect Supabase"). Set them only to run CronCal without its setup
# screens, as on Vercel. Copy this file to .env.local, which git ignores.

# ─── Your Supabase project ───────────────────────────────────────────
# All three, or CronCal names the ones missing. The secret key never reaches
# the browser: CronCal reads it on the server only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://abcdefghijklmnopqrst.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# On the web only: 12 characters or more, asked for when the account is
# made, so the first stranger to find the address can't make it.
# SETUP_CODE=

# ─── Where CronCal keeps its settings ─────────────────────────────────
# Instead of ~/Library/Application Support/CronCal, %LOCALAPPDATA%\CronCal
# or ~/.config/croncal. `npm run develop` sets it to .dev-data.
# CRONCAL_DATA_DIR=

# ─── Google Calendar ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Google Cloud OAuth client, instead of the one saved in Settings.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=....apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Only behind a proxy: the callback address Google sees.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=
